================================================================
DATASETS
================================================================

The Si.EVE chat filter's match content (its slur and phrase lexicon) is
likewise in-house data hand-authored by MSTRJK Creative Solutions & Careers
from its own chat data. It is not derived from any third-party dataset.

The only third-party datasets Verité touches are used to build the Si.EVE
tokenizer's word-frequency and register statistics, described below. Only
aggregate per-word statistics are derived and shipped; no source document text
is reproduced, redistributed, or embedded, and only sources under broad,
permissive licenses (CC0, CC-BY, CC-BY-SA / GFDL, ODC-By, Apache-2.0, MIT) are
used.

The Si.EVE tokenizer's multilingual word-frequency and register lexicon (the
per-language statistics packed into the shipped dictionary asset) was harvested
from the HPLT v3 web corpus. Only aggregate per-word statistics (occurrence and
sentence-presence counts, and averaged web-register shares) are derived and
shipped; no source document text is reproduced, redistributed, or embedded.
   HPLT v3 (HPLT/HPLT3.0)
   Provider: HPLT project (High Performance Language Technologies)
   License: Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (CC0, public domain dedication)
   https://hplt-project.org
   https://data.hplt-project.org/three/

The Si.EVE filter's word-segmentation frequency table blends that in-house
data with the word-frequency data carried by wordninja (see ALGORITHMS &
CODE HERITAGE below), whose frequency lists derive from:
   - Wikipedia / Wikimedia (English word-frequency ranks)
     https://dumps.wikimedia.org
   - Leipzig Corpora Collection (Spanish word-frequency data)
     https://wortschatz.uni-leipzig.de/en/download

The Unicode confusable/homoglyph fold table (confusables.txt) is built from
Unicode Technical Standard #39 (Unicode Security Mechanisms), (c) Unicode, Inc.
   https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr39/


