NO-TRAIN DISCLAIMER
================================================================

Verité ships no machine-learning model. The Si.EVE chat filter is a
lexicon- and rules-based system; its match content is in-house data
hand-authored by MSTRJK Creative Solutions & Careers.

No Verité machine-learning model was trained, fine-tuned, or otherwise produced
from any of the third-party datasets listed in this document. Those datasets
were used only to build the Si.EVE tokenizer's aggregate word statistics; no
dataset content is reproduced, redistributed, or embedded in the shipped
product, and only aggregate per-word statistics are derived from them.

Only sources under broad, permissive licenses were ever downloaded or used;
any source without a clearly permissive license was deliberately excluded. To
the best of MSTRJK Creative Solutions & Careers' knowledge, Verité contains no
direct infringement of any listed work; each is credited here purely as an
acknowledgement of the resources involved during development.


================================================================
ALGORITHMS & CODE HERITAGE
================================================================

wordninja (keredson/wordninja)
   The probabilistic word-segmentation algorithm (unigram-cost dynamic
   programming) used by the Si.EVE filter's de-obfuscation pass is ported
   from wordninja, and wordninja's word-frequency data (Wikipedia- and
   Leipzig-derived, see DATASETS above) is blended into the filter's
   segmentation table alongside the in-house lexicon.
   https://github.com/keredson/wordninja

Fritsch-Carlson monotone cubic interpolation
   The monotone score-to-multiplier curve used by the trust system is a
   standard published numerical method (Fritsch & Carlson, 1980). It is a
   mathematical technique, not code taken from any specific project.

VLEX9 dictionary codec
   The Si.EVE tokenizer's shipped dictionary uses an in-house binary format
   built by MSTRJK Creative Solutions & Careers. Its design draws on standard,
   published data-compression techniques, used as general methods rather than
   as code from any specific project: asymmetric numeral systems (rANS) range
   coding, front-coded and restart-indexed key blocks (SSTable-style), a static
   phrase substitution code (FSST-style), joint vector quantization for the
   register vectors, and SipHash-2-4 for the exact hot-word index. These are
   mathematical and algorithmic techniques; no third-party codec code is
   included.

LiteBans
   The Veritesauver moderation command grammar and Entry record shape are
   modelled on the LiteBans command syntax so that staff muscle memory
   carries over. Verité shares no code with LiteBans; only the command
   conventions are mirrored.

bStats
   Anonymous usage metrics are collected via the bStats library.
   https://bstats.org


